    "problem_statement": "# Issues with class pickling in cloudpickle\n\n### What happened?\n\nI've encountered two issues when pickling classes with cloudpickle:\n\n1. When pickling classes with slots, the slot attributes are not properly preserved. Instead of removing the slot attributes from the class dictionary, they're being set to None.\n\n2. When pickling ABC classes, the registry order seems to be incorrect. The ABC registry information is not being properly preserved during pickling/unpickling.\n\n### What did you expect to happen?\n\n1. For classes with slots, the slot attributes should be removed from the class dictionary during pickling, not set to None.\n\n2. For ABC classes, the registry information should be correctly preserved, maintaining the proper order of elements.\n\n### Minimal Complete Verifiable Example\n\nFor the slots issue:\n```python\nimport cloudpickle\n\nclass ClassWithSlots:\n    __slots__ = ['registered_attribute']\n    \n    def __init__(self):\n        self.registered_attribute = 42\n\n# Pickle and unpickle\nobj = ClassWithSlots()\npickled = cloudpickle.dumps(obj)\nunpickled = cloudpickle.loads(pickled)\n\n# Try to access the attribute\nprint(unpickled.registered_attribute)  # Should be 42\n```\n\nFor the ABC issue:\n```python\nimport abc\nimport cloudpickle\n\n# Create an ABC class\nMyClass = abc.ABCMeta('MyClass', (), {})\n\n# Create a related class and register it\nclass MyRelatedClass:\n    pass\nMyClass.register(MyRelatedClass)\n\n# Pickle and unpickle\npickled = cloudpickle.dumps(MyClass)\nunpickled = cloudpickle.loads(pickled)\n\n# Check if the relationship is preserved\nprint(issubclass(MyRelatedClass, unpickled))  # Should be True\n```\n\n### Relevant log output\n\nFor the slots issue, the attribute access fails after unpickling.\n\nFor the ABC issue, the issubclass check may return False after unpickling, indicating that the registry information was not properly preserved.\n\n### Anything else we need to know?\n\nThe issues appear to be in the `_class_getstate` function in cloudpickle.py, specifically in how it handles slots and ABC registries."
